CNS3D: tests of the recovered program

Build

  gfortran -std=legacy -fno-automatic -o cns3d cns3d.f

-fno-automatic keeps local variables between calls, as the 1986 compiler did.

Input

  unit 5   control cards (Appendix A): NLIMT, IG (1 laminar, 2 k-epsilon), ISWP, ITT; eight relaxation
           factors ALU ALV ALW ALP ALK ALE ALVIS ALC; RENL, DTT (DTT = 0 for steady flow)
  unit 8   restart file: L,M,N and the blocked box L1,L2,M1,M2,N1,N2 as FORMAT(9I5), then for K, I: a
           (//) record and M records (3F8.4,3E12.4,2X,6E11.4) of X Y Z U V W P TM DK DE and two unused
  unit 7   the solution, in the same format; it can be used as the next restart file

test/restart.f writes field.txt (header line, then X Y Z U V W DK DE per node) as the unit 8 file.

The listing is set up for the report's case D. DIRCOS flags walls at J=1, J=M and K=N, and the box
L1..L2, M1..M2, N1..N2 from the restart file. SYMOUT makes K=1 a symmetry plane and corrects V at the
outlet I=L against the inlet mass flow (in case D the flow leaves along y). The main program zeroes the
velocity on flagged nodes, so a moving wall must not be flagged.

Other cases need these set up again, as Appendix A expects. test/case.py makes such a copy of cns3d.f;
each edit must match exactly once, and the list of edits is printed:

  dims=LO,MO,NO  array sizes        walls=COND  faces flagged as walls in DIRCOS
  2d             K=N mirrors K=N-1 like K=1 (use N=4: with N=3 the pressure block correction is empty)
  outlet=u       the outlet corrects U, and sums the outlet flow over the same cells as the inlet
                 (the listing sums J=2..M-1, K=2..N-1, the inlet J=2..M, K=2..N)
  outlet=none    I=L is a fixed boundary
  bounc          BOUNC passes each wall's own link coefficient (see note 2)
  wallvis        SOLVEQ DO 22 sets the viscosity on all nodes (see note 1)
  pe10           link diffusion max(D, |C|/10) instead of max(D, |C|/2): central differencing up to
                 cell Peclet 10, the report's second scheme as we read it (SOLVEQ)
  erext=E        the convergence tolerance EREXT (1.E-3 in the listing)
  outletsum      the outlet flow summed over the cells of the inlet sum (BC)
  tmsource       the temperature source: the time term only (SOLVEQ, BC)
  tmcross        the cross-derivative diffusion for TM on nonorthogonal grids (SOLVEQ)
  wallk          near-wall K keeps its time and cross-derivative terms (WALLFN)

