Notes on the program as printed

These are in the listing (checked on the scan) and are kept in cns3d.f.

1. SOLVEQ, DO 22: F1 = VISE/SIGF is set on interior nodes only, so the viscosity on a wall face is half
   the fluid's, and the laminar wall shear (including that of a moving lid) is halved. With wall
   functions (IG = 2) BOUNC replaces this link. Case A suggests the report used a version without this.

2. BOUNC passes AN(I,J,K) to WALLFN for all six wall directions, so for south, east, west, top and
   bottom walls the north link is changed instead of the wall link. Case C does not converge and gives
   twice the report's reattachment length; with each wall's own link it converges near the report.

3. The outlet sums the flow over J=2..M-1, K=2..N-1 and the inlet over J=2..M, K=2..N. In case D the
   missing cells are at walls and carry little flow.

4. SOLVEQ: ANAB includes APO(I,J,K), and SP includes -APO*TJO through SPK = -CPO-APO, so the diagonal
   carries APO + APO*TJO while the source carries APO*TJO*FO. Time steps then pull the velocity toward
   zero and a steady state is not kept. Without the APO in ANAB (option unsteady) the transient
   tests above behave.

5. The temperature equation is a stub: the TM-SOURCE branch is empty (4 CONTINUE, GO TO 60), so TM is
   solved with the source left by the W equation; it also uses ISWW, ALW and ERRW. Completed in
   cns3d_fixed.f (option tmsource), which is new code.

6. WALLFN, K: near a wall SU is set to (CPO+APO)*K plus the wall production, dropping the
   cross-derivative terms of K and taking the time term at the new K, so the time derivative cancels
   in wall cells. Corrected in cns3d_fixed.f (option wallk); the steady case C is unchanged (Xr =
   4.32h). Restarting case C from its steady state with DTT = 0.1 for 3 steps changes k by at most
   0.00045 with the correction and 0.00073 without (k up to 0.065).

7. LINERX, block correction: the correction of each I plane is copied from J = JS+1 and K = KS+1
   on, so the first row and plane keep the value of the corner only. It affects only the start of
   the line iterations. The work arrays A, B, C, D are dimensioned 20 while the P equation runs I
   to L; the dims option of case.py enlarges them.

